    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_3C4qiwbWK4gkg06",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID46",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Q19-qwen3-embedding-8b__bge-reranker-v2-m3-chunk_9736e15ea4d8d2bba844c7f3",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>1.2 incitement and encouragement of harm</strong> – Encouragement, justification, or normalization of causing harm to women or gendered subjects.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: 2. SOCIETAL CONTEXT AND ROOT CAUSES OF CYBER VIOLENCE AND HATE SPEECH ONLINE AGAINST WOMEN > 2.1.2. Normalisation and invisibility of online cyber violence against women\n\n<sup>40</sup> Rape culture is defined as “the complex of beliefs that encourages male sexual aggression and supports violence against women. It is a society where violence is seen as sexy and sexuality as violent. In a rape culture women perceive a continuum of threatened violence that ranges from sexual remarks to sexual touching to rape itself.”, in Buchwald, E., Fletcher P.R., Roth, M. (2005), “Transforming a Rape Culture”, Milkweed Editions, Minneapolis.</div><br>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q19-qwen3-embedding-8b__bge-reranker-v2-m3-chunk_9736e15ea4d8d2bba844c7f3",
