      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>2.1 descriptive attacks</strong> – Negative descriptive generalizations about women or gendered groups.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: 4. Towards common definitions of cyber violence against women and girls > Proposed definition\n\nOnline gender-based hate speech is defined as content posted and shared through ICT means that:\n\nis hateful towards women and/or girls because of their gender, or because of a combination of gender and other factors (e.g. race, age, disability, sexuality, ethnicity, nationality, religion or profession); and/or\n\nspreads, incites, promotes or justifies hatred based on gender, or because of a combi- nation of gender and other factors (e.g. race, age, disability, sexuality, ethnicity, nationality, religion or profession).</div><br>",
