    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_3C4qiwbWK4gkg06",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID64",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Q40-all-chunk_1713bcff2114a70bef1ace47",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks</strong> – Aggressive, degrading, or emotionally hostile insults against women, feminists, or gendered subjects.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: 2. SOCIETAL CONTEXT AND ROOT CAUSES OF CYBER VIOLENCE AND HATE SPEECH ONLINE AGAINST WOMEN > 2.3. The architecture of cyber spaces and women’s victimisation > 2.3.3. Mob mentality\n\nGender trolling attacks are precipitated by women asserting their opinions online;\n\nThey feature graphic sexualised and gender-based insults;\n\nThey include rape and death threats — often credible ones — and frequently involve real-life targeting, which adds to the credibility of the threats;\n\nThey cross multiple social media or online platforms;\n\nThey occur at unusually high levels of intensity and frequency (numerous threats or messages per day or even per hour);\n\nThey are perpetuated for an unusual duration (months or even years);\n\nThey involve many attackers in a concerted and often coordinated campaign.</div><br>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q40-all-chunk_1713bcff2114a70bef1ace47",
