      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks</strong> – Aggressive, degrading, or emotionally hostile insults against women, feminists, or gendered subjects.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: 2. SOCIETAL CONTEXT AND ROOT CAUSES OF CYBER VIOLENCE AND HATE SPEECH ONLINE AGAINST WOMEN > 3.2. The impact of cyber violence and hate speech online against women > 3.3.1. Types of online platforms where perpetrations occur\n\nTwo reports point at Twitter’s specific nature that leads to an overload of violent content aimed directly at individual women. The Demos “Misogyny on Twitter” report published in 2014 reveals for example that “of over 100,000 Tweets mentioning ‘rape’ between 26th December 2013 and 9th February\n\n<sup>95</sup> Code of Conduct on countering illegal hate speech online (2018), “Results of the 3rd monitoring exercise”, available at http://ec.europa.eu/newsroom/just/item-detail.cfm?item_id=612086</div><br>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
