        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>2.3 dehumanising attacks &amp; overt sexual objectification</strong> – Dehumanization, animalization, sexual objectification, or reduction of women to sexual or body objects.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: REFERENCES\n\nINHOPE (2017), Facts, Figures & Trends, “The fight against online Child Sexual Abuse in perspective”, available at http://www.inhope.org/tns/resources/statistics-and-infographics/statistics-and-infographics-2017.aspx\n\n<u>Inter Parliamentary Union (2016), “Sexism, harassment and violence against women</u> parliamentarians”, Issues Brief, Oct. 2016, available at http://archive.ipu.org/pdf/publications/issuesbrief-e.pdf</div><br>",
