    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_3C4qiwbWK4gkg06",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID87",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Q67-qwen3-embedding-8b__bge-reranker-v2-m3-chunk_24a4f2a69be82e6cf034cdf3",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>3.1 casual use of gendered slurs, profanities, and insults</strong> – Casual or normalized use of gendered slurs, profanity, and insults.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: FORMS OF ONLINE GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE > 5 GENDER-BASED HATE SPEECH\n\nGender-based hate speech includes hurtful, harmful, hateful, insulting, demeaning, shaming, and vitriolic statements, comments, or other forms of expression that target a person for their sex, gender, or sexual orientation; and includes comments suggesting that the person targeted deserves to face harm or should harm themselves.<sup>27</sup>\n\n<sup>27</sup> https://asiapacific.unwomen.org/sites/default/files/Field%2000ffice%2020ESEAsia/Docs/Publications/2020/12/ap-ICT-VAWG-report-7Dec20.pdf\n\nillustration: stylized figures holding smartphones</div><br>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
