    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_3C4qiwbWK4gkg06",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID123",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "Q103-qwen3-embedding-8b__bge-reranker-v2-m3-chunk_947d30c2933294cd036075b5",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice</strong> – Paternalistic, condescending, or unsolicited advice based on gender stereotypes.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: Illustrative Gender Stereotypes and Gender Discriminatory Roles\n\nMen’s social standing and reputation as upheld by the loyalty, obedience and fidelity of their female spouses, siblings and children, the absence of which may be a justification for violence.\n\nMen considered as effeminate and weak if they are gender egalitarian or support feminist movements.\n\nNotions of femininity based on passivity, vulnerability, purity and heterosexuality.\n\nWomen who assert, speak out, or defend equal rights as ‘man-hating’ or unwomanly.\n\nLesbian, bisexual, and transgender women as outside the feminine ‘norm’ and as needing policing/ correction.</div><br>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q103-qwen3-embedding-8b__bge-reranker-v2-m3-chunk_947d30c2933294cd036075b5",
