      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<p><strong>EDOS Label</strong></p><p><strong>4.1 supporting mistreatment of individual women</strong> – Justifying, minimizing, or normalizing mistreatment of individual women, including victim blaming.</p><br><p><strong>Paragraph</strong></p><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Section: 2. SOCIETAL CONTEXT AND ROOT CAUSES OF CYBER VIOLENCE AND HATE SPEECH ONLINE AGAINST WOMEN > 2.2. Gender imbalance in the tech sector trickles down\n\n<sup>41</sup> <u>Powell, A. (2016), “Be careful posting images online’ is just another form of modern-day victim-blaming”, The Conversation, available at</u> http://theconversation.com/be-careful-posting-images-online-is-just-another-form-of-modern-day-victim-blaming-64116\n\n<sup>42</sup> Ibid.\n\n<sup>43</sup> Amnesty International (2018), Toxic Twitter, a toxic place for women, available at https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/research/2018/03/online-violence-against-women-chapter-1/</div><br>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "Q118-bge-m3__qwen3-reranker-8b-chunk_b6d1fd2024fe15487a33c3a4",
